# Class: obo:MSIO_0000169 (petri dish)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:MSIO_0000169 " a petri dish is a container used to grow cells or perform biochemical reactions, which used to be made of glass, but which is now available in a variety of surface treated or non-treated plastic polymers. a petri dish is a thin cylinder with the upper part acting as a lid, resting on small peg, large enough to enable gaseaous exchanges but still preventing water evaporation."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:MSIO_0000169 "Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en)
